---
/**
 * Terms of use, EN. Twin of `src/pages/conditions-utilisation.astro`.
 *
 * Carries the mandatory statement from `docs/CLAUDE.md`: advertising and
 * referral service, independent contractor, no technical or engineering advice.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { pathFor } from '@lib/routes.ts';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '@lib/schema.ts';

const locale = 'en' as const;
const ref = { type: 'static', page: 'terms' } as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  locale={locale}
  ref={ref}
  title="Terms of use — Solage Capitale"
  description="Solage Capitale is an advertising and referral service. What the site does, what it does not do, and who you are actually contracting with for work."
  schema={[
    breadcrumbSchema(locale, [
      { name: "Home", ref: { type: 'home' } },
      { name: "Terms of use", ref },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <section class="contenant bloc-page">
    <div class="mesure">
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>

      <p class="chapeau">
        Read this before using the form. It states exactly what this service is, what it is not,
        and who you are committing to if work goes ahead.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site is</h2>
      <p>
        Solage Capitale is an <strong>advertising and referral service</strong>. It publishes
        information about foundation problems in the Quebec City region and passes reader
        enquiries on to a contractor.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Solage Capitale performs no construction work.</strong> It does not excavate,
        install drains, inject cracks or apply membranes. It employs no contractor and
        supervises no site.
      </p>

      <h2>Who you contract with</h2>
      <p>
        The provider who calls you back is an <strong>independent company</strong>, separate
        from Solage Capitale, holding its own licence from the Régie du bâtiment du Québec. Any
        contract, quote or warranty is formed <strong>between you and that company</strong>,
        never with Solage Capitale.
      </p>
      <p>
        You remain free to decline, to seek other quotes, and to verify the licence of anyone
        who comes to your home. That is your right, and this site encourages you to exercise it:
        <a href={pathFor({ type: 'static', page: 'faq' }, locale)}>how to check an RBQ
        licence</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>No technical advice</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site constitutes <strong>technical advice, a diagnosis or an engineering
        opinion</strong>. The pages explain general phenomena, the applicable regulations and
        what a professional does. They replace neither an inspection of your building nor the
        judgement of an engineer or building technologist.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site deliberately provides <strong>no execution instructions</strong>. Excavating
        against a foundation, injecting a crack or applying a membrane are works that bear on
        personal safety and structural integrity: they belong to a licensed contractor.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy of the information</h2>
      <p>
        Regulatory facts are tied to their public source and dated. They can change. Where no
        primary source exists for a figure, the site says so rather than publishing one — which
        is the case for price ranges, as explained on the
        <a href={pathFor({ type: 'static', page: 'pricing' }, locale)}>pricing page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        The information is provided as is, with no warranty of completeness. Solage Capitale
        cannot be held responsible for decisions taken on the basis of the site's content, nor
        for the execution, quality or price of work carried out by a third-party company.
        Remedies relating to work are exercised against the company that performed it.
      </p>

      <h2>Ownership</h2>
      <p>
        The site's text and diagrams are its own property. Photographs come from freely licensed
        archives; their provenance and licence are recorded and travel with the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law and changes</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the law applicable in Quebec. They may be amended; the
        version displayed is the one that applies. Use of the site constitutes acceptance.
      </p>

      <h2>Your information</h2>
      <p>
        How information submitted through the form is handled is described in the
        <a href={pathFor({ type: 'static', page: 'privacy' }, locale)}>privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
